&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who loves the craft of compensation, thinks like a business leader, and gets excited about building something better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Compensation Strategy &amp;amp; Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the evolution of our global compensation philosophy, job architecture, leveling, and pay structures to support a high-performance organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring a strong point of view on compensation investment, balancing market dynamics, internal equity, business priorities, and long-term financial sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape our broader Total Rewards strategy, ensuring compensation works alongside benefits, recognition, and the overall employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Equity &amp;amp; Long-Term Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our equity compensation strategy, including new-hire grants, refresh programs, long-term incentives, and retention approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the&amp;nbsp; multi-year equity models and budget,&amp;nbsp; taking into consideration burn rate, dilution, and future investment needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape senior leadership compensation strategy and support Compensation Committee preparation, governance, and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Strategic Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to People Leaders on critical hiring decisions, retention challenges, organizational changes, and compensation investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Talent Acquisition to ensure our compensation approach supports the talent we want to attract and reinforces what makes Klaviyo a compelling place to grow a career.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Team Leadership &amp;amp; Operating Model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a high-performing compensation team, strengthening technical capabilities, business judgment, and a culture of ownership and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rethink how compensation work gets done, using technology, automation, and AI to simplify processes, improve insights, and increase the team&#39;s impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive compensation experience, including significant leadership responsibility within a high-growth technology company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of proven success leading and developing a compensation team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing, transforming, or meaningfully evolving global compensation strategies and programs within a publicly traded company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial and analytical capabilities, including equity modeling, burn rate, dilution, long-term incentive design, and compensation budget planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with executive compensation, Compensation Committee support, public-company governance, and regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of pay equity and evolving pay transparency requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience extending compensation frameworks into new markets as a company scales, balancing global consistency with local market realities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with compensation systems, market data platforms, and analytics, along with demonstrated experience in using AI and automation to improve how work gets done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs other related duties, as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
