&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Klaviyo, we value the unique backgrounds, experiences and perspectives each Klaviyo (we call ourselves Klaviyos) brings to our workplace each and every day. We believe everyone deserves a fair shot at success and appreciate the experiences each person brings beyond the traditional job requirements. If you’re a close but not exact match with the description, we hope you’ll still consider applying. Want to learn more about life at Klaviyo? Visit &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://klaviyo.com/careers&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;klaviyo.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;to see how we empower creators to own their own destiny.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join the Mobile App Growth team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Mobile App Growth team&#39;s mission is to enable Klaviyo customers to develop and maintain personalized relationships with their mobile app users through rich mobile app experiences. The team is part of the Mobile App Marketing org and owns Klaviyo&#39;s mobile SDKs — the foundational layer that enables customers to integrate Klaviyo into their mobile apps. We maintain native and wrapper SDKs across iOS, Android, React Native, Expo, and Flutter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a natural extension of the SDK, the team also builds and maintains adjacent mobile products that are enabled by it:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-app messaging — including the in-app messaging publishing and scheduling pipeline&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Universal linking — universal links settings pages and web tier&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Geofencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That product list keeps expanding — this year alone the team is greenfielding several new features, including mobile inbox. We&#39;re looking for passionate engineers who want to roll up their sleeves and grow beyond just Android into the other areas the team owns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is open to fully remote work from within The United States&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you&#39;ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and ship features and fixes to the Android SDK — your primary area of ownership — used across a huge range of third-party apps and OS versions/devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pitch in on our other mobile SDKs (iOS, React Native, Expo, and Flutter) when priorities call for it; you don&#39;t need to be an expert everywhere, but you should be willing to get hands-on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the backend services, infrastructure, and embedded web UI that power products like in-app messaging, universal linking, and geofencing — including newer greenfield work like mobile inbox.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose and resolve SDK issues reported by customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, well-tested code and participate in code and design review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product and other engineering teams to keep tracking and messaging behavior consistent across platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to documentation, sample apps, and integration guides that customers use to adopt the SDKs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Android-first&lt;/strong&gt; — 1-3 years of professional Android development experience, ideally including Kotlin; this is your core strength and primary focus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-motivated &lt;/strong&gt;— you don&#39;t need heavy oversight to make progress; you take a problem, figure out the right questions, and drive it to done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High ownership&lt;/strong&gt; — you treat outcomes as yours end-to-end, not just the code you personally typed. As AI tooling raises how much one engineer can credibly own, this matters more than it used to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptable&lt;/strong&gt; — willing to pick up iOS, backend, or frontend work when it falls under the team&#39;s ownership; you don&#39;t need to be an expert everywhere.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production-tested&lt;/strong&gt; — experience shipping and maintaining production Android code, with a solid grasp of the Android lifecycle, threading, and Gradle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comfortable in the weeds&lt;/strong&gt; — used to debugging across a wide matrix of devices, OS versions, and third-party app environments, since SDK work means you don&#39;t control the host app.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality-minded &lt;/strong&gt;— familiar with testing practices (unit, integration, instrumentation) and CI/CD for mobile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clear communicator&lt;/strong&gt; — you&#39;ll work with customers&#39; engineering teams as well as your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curious&lt;/strong&gt; — comfortable with webviews and location services, and open to picking up new technologies (Python, React, AWS) as the team&#39;s surface area grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus&lt;/strong&gt;: experience building or maintaining an SDK/library (versus an app), exposure to iOS/Swift or backend services, familiarity with push notification/messaging systems, or contributions to open source.&lt;/li&gt;
